en":["06"]},"Don’t rely on vitamin C to prevent colds"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"Don’t get a whole-body PET-CT or tumor marker panel if you have no symptoms"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"Don’t expect fitness trackers or smartwatches to help you lose weight"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"Don’t pay a premium for organic food just to be “healthier”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-10"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"Don’t spend a lot of money on health supplements, herbal formulas, or tonics to “improve your health”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-11"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["11"]},"Don’t take probiotics long-term if you have no gut problems"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-12"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["12"]},"Don’t force yourself to take cold showers just to “boost immunity”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-13"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["13"]},"Don’t buy products marketed for detox, colon cleansing, enzymes, or alkaline water"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-14"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["14"]},"Don’t force yourself to drink water just to hit “8 glasses a day”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-15"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["15"]},"Don’t spend money on fortune‑telling, tarot, or astrology to make decisions"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-16"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["16"]},"Don’t buy blue-light-blocking glasses to “protect your vision,” and don’t believe claims that staring at screens for months will ruin your eyes — but severe eye pain, redness, and swelling require immediate medical attention"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-17"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["17"]},"Don’t treat blood donation as a health habit: claims that it “detoxifies, lowers cholesterol, and prevents heart attacks” lack randomized trial support, while frequent donation truly causes iron deficiency"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-18"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["18"]},"Don’t rely on generic health check packages to prevent disease; instead, get the evidence‑based screenings appropriate for your age and gender"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-19"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["19"]},"Don’t start taking uric‑acid‑lowering drugs just because a checkup shows high uric acid but you’ve never had symptoms"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-20"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["20"]},"Don’t have a gallbladder removed prophylactically just because an ultrasound found gallstones but you’ve never felt any pain"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-21"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["21"]},"Don’t cut calcium out to prevent kidney stones"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-22"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["22"]},"Don’t buy crystals, bracelets, or Pixiu figurines for “good luck,” “wealth attraction,” or “health benefits”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/06-23","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["23"]},"Don’t expect shopping to lift your mood or boost your sense of self-worth"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-24"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["24"]},"Don’t spend extra money to “move up a rung” among your peers by buying a new house, car, or social circle"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-25"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["25"]},"Don’t believe that “willpower is like a muscle that runs out after use”"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-26"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["26"]},"Don’t expect skipping breakfast or the 16:8 intermittent fasting method to help you control your weight; instead, pick a meal timing you can stick to long-term"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-27"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["27"]},"Do not believe that \"masturbation harms the body\" or that \"abstinence is the only way to improve\"; what truly matters is whether it interferes with your sleep, work, and relationships"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-28"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["28"]},"Do not spend money on \"conversion therapy\" or \"gay علاج,\" and do not send your family members to undergo it either"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-29"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["29"]},"Do not expect “correct lifting posture” or lifting training to prevent back pain; reduce the weight and number of lifts, and exercise regularly"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-30"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["30"]},"Do not expect extra calcium or bone broth to make a fracture heal faster"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/06-31"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["31"]},"Don’t rely on an AI chatbot alone to judge a medical or legal problem; before seeing a doctor, going to court or spending big money, find the source it cites and check it against the original"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/06"},"children":["Chapter 6"," ·"," ","Items to avoid"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"06-23"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["23"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-b"},"children":["Evidence"," ","B"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["Don’t expect shopping to lift your mood or boost your sense of self-worth"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["On average, people who place a higher value on money and material possessions report lower levels of happiness. This conclusion comes from a meta-analysis of 259 separate studies, though the link between the two is fairly weak and it’s unclear which factor drives the other. Other research comparing spending on experiences versus physical goods found that money spent on experiences tends to bring more satisfaction. So when you’re in a bad mood, reallocating your budget toward a day out or a meal with friends is far more likely to help than adding more items to your shopping cart."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No cost at all. The hard part is resisting the urge to buy…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["This meta-analysis combined data from 259 independent studies, covering a total of 753 effect sizes. The resul…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: Don’t expect shopping to lift your mood or boost your sense of self-worth"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["No cost at all. The hard part is resisting the urge to buy things when you’re feeling down."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["This meta-analysis combined data from 259 independent studies, covering a total of 753 effect sizes. The results showed that individuals who prioritize material possessions tend to report lower happiness levels. On the most commonly used multi-dimensional well‑being scale, the correlation coefficient was r = –0.19 (adjusted ρ = –0.24). When only the single dimension of “valuing money” was measured, the correlation weakened to r = –0.08 to –0.11. The strength of this link varied depending on the specific outcome measured: it was strongest with risky health‑related and consumption behaviors and negative self‑evaluations (r = –0.28 to –0.44) and weakest with overall life satisfaction and negative emotions (r = –0.13 to –0.15). Mediation analyses suggested that this negative relationship may arise because psychological needs remain unmet. Another set of studies asked different groups of participants whether spending on experiences or on goods made them happier; respondents consistently chose experiences. Laboratory experiments confirmed this: recalling a purchase made for an experience produced a better mood than recalling a purchase of a physical item. Both studies used overseas samples, so these findings don’t apply to the Chinese population."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["Dittmar H, Bond R, Hurst M, Kasser T (2014). The relationship between materialism and personal well-being: A meta-analysis. Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 107(5), 879-924. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1037/a0037409","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1037/a0037409"]},"；Van Boven L, Gilovich T (2003). To do or to have? That is the question. Journal of Personality and Social Psychology, 85(6), 1193-1202. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1037/0022-3514.85.6.1193","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1037/0022-3514.85.6.1193"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1037/a0037409","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["Caveats: Most of the included studies surveyed the same group of people at a single point in time, so they can’t determine which factor comes first. The authors themselves note that further experiments and long‑term follow‑ups are needed to clarify the direction of this relationship. Therefore, this recommendation should not be interpreted as “shopping makes people unhappy”; rather, it means “relying on shopping to improve your mood is unlikely to succeed.” The overall correlation is modest: r = –0.19 accounts for only a few percentage points of variation, and individual differences are considerable. Since both studies used foreign samples, there are no comparable Chinese data to cite. This advice does not discourage spending on items you genuinely enjoy; it simply warns against using shopping as a mood‑regulation tool, as that can lead to repeated impulse buys when you’re feeling down. Specific ways to save money are described in Section 5. Evidence‑based strategies for coping with low mood can be found in the latter part of Section 22 and in Section 29. Information on budgeting to “outperform” others is covered in Item 24 of this section."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"